  "worked_solution": "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nC∧(C∨B)≡C.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $C.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $C.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∧(B∨C) & ≡B≢C.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $C.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∧(B∨C) & ≡C∧(C∨B) \\\\  & ≡C.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
